      "content": "It is incredibly difficult to feel like your life was a lie, but the way you feel is a direct result of a profound betrayal, not a permanent reflection of your worth. The \"void\" you describe is a heavy aftermath of hope and effort being shattered, but it does not erase the value of the sacrifices you made or the strength it took to face the truth. You might feel like you have no future to do it for, but the \"recovery\" of self is not just about the \"better self self\" one was before the lie; it is about who you become when you realize you have to rebuild without the support of a follower self that no longer exists. This is a journey that is not about \"trying again\" but about \"starting over\" with the knowledge that your life was never that fragile to begin with.",
